    "result": "All tests are now passing! Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **finetune/index.js** - Missing named exports\nThe test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. I added named exports for the constants:\n```javascript\nexport { APPROVAL_STATUSES, DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS, GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS, RISK_LEVELS };\n```\n\n### 2. **eval/metrics.js** - toxicityMetric parameter handling\nThe `toxicityMetric` function was being called by `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`, but the function signature expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. I fixed it to intelligently detect whether the second parameter is:\n- A list of banned terms (single lowercase words with no spaces) \u2192 use as banned terms\n- References (mixed case content) \u2192 use default banned terms\n\nThis maintains backward compatibility while fixing the test failure.\n\n**Test Results:** All 28 tests across 8 test files now pass \u2713\n\nPublic API exports remain intact and accessible through the namespace (`Finetune.APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `Eval.toxicityMetric`, etc.).",
